and DomainError::render() (verified against michi's real source, crates/michi-core/src/error.rs and hints.rs, at the pinned rev per AC-015) writes message as a single raw `message: {text}
` line and writes hints, separately, via append_hints() as a COUNTED block -- `help[{hints.len()}]:
` followed by exactly hints.len() lines, each `  {hint}
` (two-space indented) -- with no newline sanitization applied to either. An un-flattened multi-line message therefore emits extra physical lines carrying no `message:`/`help[`/`  ` prefix at all, indistinguishable from whatever block follows; an un-flattened multi-line hint desynchronizes the count render() already declared in `help[N]:` from the number of physical lines that actually follow it, since N is fixed at hints.len() (the number of Hint values passed in) before any individual hint's own embedded newlines are considered -- a line-oriented parser reading exactly N declared hint lines would read past the intended block into that hint's own later lines, or (for the last hint) into whatever comes after the hints block entirely.

